.Dd June 1, 2025
.Dt XO_DISCARDING_OUTPUT 3
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm xo_discarding_output , xo_discarding_output_h
.Nd test whether libxo is permanently filtering the current output position
.Sh LIBRARY
.Lb libxo
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In libxo/xo.h
.Ft int
.Fn xo_discarding_output "void"
.Ft int
.Fn xo_discarding_output_h "xo_handle_t *xop"
.Sh DESCRIPTION
When a filter is in place, some output positions may be permanently
filtered out: the active filter has determined that no content
generated at the current position can ever appear in the final output.
.Pp
The
.Fn xo_discarding_output
function returns true when the current output position of the default
handle is in this permanently-discarded state
.Pq Dv XO_STATUS_DEAD .
Callers can use this to skip expensive computation that would
otherwise precede a call to
.Xr xo_emit 3 .
.Pp
The
.Fn xo_discarding_output_h
variant operates on the specified handle.
To use the default handle, pass a
.Dv NULL
handle.
.Pp
Both functions return false (proceed normally) when:
.Bl -bullet -compact
.It
filtering is disabled,
.It
the filter module is not loaded, or
.It
the filter status is anything other than
.Dv XO_STATUS_DEAD
(for example
.Dv XO_STATUS_TRACK
or
.Dv XO_STATUS_PRED ,
which still require key and predicate fields to be evaluated before
a decision can be made).
.El
.Sh RETURN VALUES
Returns true
.Pq non-zero
when the current output position is permanently filtered out
.Pq Dv XO_STATUS_DEAD .
Returns false
.Pq zero
otherwise.
.Sh EXAMPLES
.Bd -literal -offset indent
xo_open_container("interface-information");
if (!xo_discarding_output()) {
    /* skip expensive work when we know output is permanently discarded */
    xo_open_container("connections");
    xo_emit("{:field/...}", value);
    xo_close_container("connections");
}
xo_close_container("interface-information");
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr libxo 3 ,
.Xr xo_add_filter 3 ,
.Xr xo_emit 3 ,
.Xr xo_filter 7
.Sh HISTORY
The
.Fn xo_discarding_output
function first appeared in
.Fx 15.0 .
